note top of AppContainer
  <b>Manual dependency injection</b>
  CampApp builds one AppContainer with the
  Firestore repositories. Each controller's
  companion factory(...) takes its repositories
  from (application as CampApp).container.
  Tests build controllers with fake repositories.
end note

note as ControllerNote
  Every <<ViewModel>> class extends androidx
  ViewModel (the controller in MVC) and has a
  companion factory(...) (Factory pattern).
  Its state is Compose mutableStateOf, so the
  screen redraws when it changes.
  suspend fetchX() is what unit tests call;
  loadX() runs it in viewModelScope.
end note

note bottom of NotificationsController
  Observer pattern: implements InboxListener,
  so the inbox updates live.
end note

note bottom of LotteryDrawer
  Takes an injected Random so tests repeat.
  The draw is a Firestore transaction, so it
  runs once even if several phones start it.
end note

note as PlannedNote
  <<planned>> classes (grey, dashed) are on the
  CRC cards but are built after the half-way
  checkpoint; their methods are from the card's
  responsibilities, not from code.
end note
@enduml
